# docs/CHANGELOG.md is generated from git history by scripts/gen-changelog.mjs. It is
# rewritten wholesale on every regeneration, so two branches that both regenerate it always
# conflict textually even though neither is wrong — the resolver's only sensible action is to
# regenerate, which the `check-changelog` gate enforces anyway.
#
# `merge=ours` tells git to keep this side's copy during a merge instead of stopping on
# conflict. That removes the one recurring conflict from this repo's workflow; the changelog is
# then regenerated by the pre-push gate from the merged history, which is the only correct content
# either way. Enable per-clone with:
#
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without that config the attribute is inert (git falls back to a normal merge), so a clone that
# has not opted in still behaves safely — it just conflicts as before.
docs/CHANGELOG.md merge=ours
